    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0503" n="399" xml:id="pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.77/95.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A request has been received from Martin W. Littleton that action on the
                    Department’s instruction to you No. 193 of February 8 be delayed until a hearing
                    on the contentions of the North Coast Railway Company can be had by the
                    Department. You will therefore suspend action until further instructed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
